# Satellite only (sd:3100): move the system and pack checkouts to the pair
# the hub-pin tag names, which the hub's last `repo-sync.sh refresh` pushed.
# Install it in `<config>/cron-jobs/jobs/<satellite host>/`;
# local-repo-sync/README.md, "Satellites follow the hub", has the steps.
#
# At the hub's pin, `follow` does nothing and drains nothing, so most runs
# cost one tag fetch. When they differ, it drains this machine's
# lanes first, waiting up to 45 minutes; JOB_TIMEOUT sits above that so the
# drain, not the job limit, decides. A slot that finds this job's own run
# still active logs `skipped` and exits 0. On the hub, `follow` says so and
# exits 0.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/5 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="55m"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-repo-sync/repo-sync.sh\" follow"
